1
00:01:34,508 --> 00:01:41,910
<v SALLY>  Good morning. Thanks for coming in to see us here at the agency, Joe. I’m one of the agency representatives, and my name’s Sally Baker.


2
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:44,852
<v JOE>   Hi Sally. I think we spoke on the phone, didn’t we?


3
00:01:44,852 --> 00:01:55,088
<v SALLY> That’s right, we did. So thank you for sending in your CV. We’ve had quite a careful look at it and I think we have two jobs that might be suitable for you.


4
00:01:55,088 --> 00:01:55,826
<v JOE>      OK.


5
00:01:55,826 --> 00:02:02,185
<v SALLY>  The first one is in a company based in North London. They’re looking for an administrative assistant.


6
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:05,326
<v JOE>    OK. What sort of company is it?


7
00:02:05,326 --> 00:02:10,542
<v SALLY> They’re called Home Solutions and they design and make furniture. 

8
00:02:10,542 --> 00:02:14,728
<v JOE>    Oh, I don’t know much about that, but it sounds interesting.


9
00:02:14,728 --> 00:02:28,676
<v SALLY>  Yes, well as I said, they want someone in their office, and looking at your past experience it does look as if you fit quite a few of the requirements. So on your CV it appears you’ve done some data entry?

10
00:02:28,676 --> 00:02:29,960
<v JOE>   Yes.


11
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:36,813
<v SALLY> So that’s one skill they want. Then they expect the person they appoint to attend meetings and take notes there …


12
00:02:36,813 --> 00:02:39,306
<v JOE>     OK. I’ve done that before, yes.


13
00:02:39,306 --> 00:02:43,182
<v SALLY>  And you’d need to be able to cope with general admin.


14
00:02:43,182 --> 00:02:50,237
<v JOE>     Filling, and keeping records and so on? That should be OK. And in my last job I also had to manage the diary.

15
00:02:50,237 --> 00:02:58,603
<v SALLY>  Excellent. That’s something they want here too. I’d suggest you add it to your CV – I don’t think you mentioned that, did you?


16
00:02:58,603 --> 00:02:59,298
<v JOE>    No.


17
00:02:59,298 --> 00:03:07,873
<v SALLY>   So as far as the requirements go, they want good computer skills, of course, and they particularly mention spreadsheets.


18
00:03:07,873 --> 00:03:09,170
<v JOE>   That should be fine.


19
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:14,501
<v SALLY>  And interpersonal skills – which would be something they’d check with your references.


20
00:03:14,501 --> 00:03:16,411
<v JOE>    I think that should be OK, yes.


21
00:03:16,411 --> 00:03:26,582
<v SALLY>  Then they mention that they want someone who is careful and takes care with details  – just looking at your CV, I’d say you’re probably alright there.


22
00:03:26,582 --> 00:03:30,940
<v JOE>   I think so, yes. Do they want any special experience?


23
00:03:30,940 --> 00:03:35,131
<v SALLY>  I think they wanted some experience of teleconferencing.


24
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:37,672
<v JOE>      I’ve got three years’ experience of that.


25
00:03:37,672 --> 00:03:47,850
<v SALLY>  let’s see, yes, good. In fact they’re only asking for at least one year, so that’s great. So is that something that might interest you?


26
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:56,062
<v JOE>    It is, yes. The only thing is, you said they were in North London so it would be quite a long commute for me.


27
00:03:56,062 --> 00:03:57,656
<v SALLY>  OK.


28
00:04:39,387 --> 00:04:46,520
<v SALLY>  So the second position might suit you better as far as the location goes; that’s for a warehouse assistant and that’s in South London.


29
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,837
<v JOE>    Yes, that would be a lot closer.


30
00:04:48,837 --> 00:04:51,588
<v SALLY>  And you’ve worked in a warehouse before, haven’t you?


31
00:04:51,588 --> 00:04:52,375
<v JOE>    Yes.


32
00:04:52,375 --> 00:05:01,076
<v SALLY> So as far as the responsibilities for this position go, they want someone who can manage the stock, obviously, and also deliveries. 

33
00:05:01,076 --> 00:05:08,390
<v JOE>    That should be OK. You’ve got to keep track of stuff, but I’ve always been quite good with numbers.


34
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:15,135
<v SALLY>   Good, that’s their first requirement. And they want someone who’s computer literate, which we know you are.


35
00:05:15,135 --> 00:05:16,021
<v JOE>      Sure.


36
00:05:16,021 --> 00:05:21,733
<v SALLY> Then they mention organisational skills. They want someone who’s well organised.


37
00:05:21,733 --> 00:05:24,260
<v JOE>   Yes, I think I am.


38
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:25,801
<v SALLY>  And tidy?

39
00:05:25,801 --> 00:05:29,272
<v JOE>   Yes, they go together really, don’t they?


40
00:05:29,272 --> 00:05:35,851
<v SALLY>  Sure. Then the usual stuff; they want someone who can communicate well both orally and in writing.


41
00:05:35,841 --> 00:05:46,576
<v JOE>  OK. And for the last warehouse job I had, one of the things I enjoyed most was being part of a team. I found that was really essential for the job.


42
00:05:46,576 --> 00:05:58,401
<v SALLY>  Excellent. Yes, they do mention that they want someone who’s used to that, yes. Now when you were working in a warehouse last time, what sorts of items were you dealing with?


43
00:05:58,401 --> 00:06:04,690
<v JOE>    It was mostly bathroom and kitchen equipment, sinks and stoves and fridges.


44
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:07,928
<v SALLY>  So you’re OK moving heavy things?


45
00:06:07,928 --> 00:06:11,746
<v JOE>    Sure. I’m quite strong, and I’ve had the training.


46
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:24,163
<v SALLY> Good. Now as far as experience goes, they mention they want someone with a licence, and that you have experience of driving in London – so you can cope with the traffic and so on.


47
00:06:24,163 --> 00:06:25,832
<v JOE>     Yes, no problem.


48
00:06:25,832 --> 00:06:35,542
<v SALLY>  And you’ve got experience of warehouse work … and the final thing they mention is customer service. I think looking at your CV you’ve OK there.


49
00:06:35,542 --> 00:06:40,416
<v JOE>     Right. So what about pay? Can you tell me a bit more about that, please …